wDOA0JFE88AAAABNeiJZQ","user":{"login":"whitelynx","id":285264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTI2NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/285264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/whitelynx","html_url":"https://github.com/whitelynx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whitelynx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whitelynx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whitelynx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whitelynx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whitelynx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whitelynx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whitelynx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whitelynx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whitelynx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-06T01:36:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-06T01:36:32Z","body":"> Discussed on Jun 11th legal call: reality of this license is there is core text, but then a large number of additional clauses (restrictions) that can be added in any combination via a modular license builder: https://firstdonoharm.dev/build\n> \n> SPDX License List cannot accommodate all these variations, but will approve the \"core\" license using the SPDX id: `Hippocratic-3.0-core` to make sure it's clear what text this is referring to. Using the full word \"Hippocratic\" to be consistent with existing `Hippocratic-2.1` already on the SPDX License List.\n> \n> Note that the many combinations that can be made via the additional clauses would be different licenses due to them being substantively different conditions on the license.\n\nFor now, would it make sense to use `WITH AdditionRef-` clauses to notate the additional modules when used in a project?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/5199399269/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/5219245154","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2931#issuecomment-5219245154","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2931","id":5219245154,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE88AAAABNxdcYg","user":{"login":"pmonks","id":54865,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0ODY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54865?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmonks","html_url":"https://github.com/pmonks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmonks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmonks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmonks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmonks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmonks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmonks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmonks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmonks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmonks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-07T15:58:19Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T15:59:18Z","body":"@whitelynx I can't answer your question directly, though that's similar to what I was proposing in my final paragraph (albeit I was proposing 16 SPDX-listed License Exceptions, rather than having to fall back on AdditionRefs).\n\nThe problem with using AdditionRefs for \"well defined\" exceptions (like the 16 that OES publish for `Hippocratic-3.0`) is that they tend to not be interoperable - every tool implementer makes up their own and then suddenly we're back to the Tower of Babel problem that SPDX addresses.  I would personally prefer to see 16 License Exceptions added to the SPDX list, rather than just kicking the can into the wild west of Refs (if that isn't too mangled a metaphor!).\n\nThe counterpoint is that OES' approach of dynamically modifying a single license text, based on any combination of those 16 clauses, is not well supported by SPDX's current approach to license text matching.  I personally view that as both a poor choice by OES, and (simultaneously) a limitation of SPDX's matching guidelines that may warrant attention at some point.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/5219245154/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/5517205743","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2931#issuecomment-5517205743","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2931","id":5517205743,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE88AAAABSNng7w","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":